.TH SONNETTE 1 2026-11-04 garnish "garnish manual"
.SH NAME
sonnette \- show a garnish VM's desktop notifications on the host
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sonnette relay \-\-cid
.I cid
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sonnette relay
is the host side of
.BR sonnette\-agent (1),
the guest's notification server. It connects to the agent of the VM at vsock
CID
.IR cid ,
shows the guest's notifications through the host's own notification server,
and sends back the actions the user picks and the notifications that close.
.PP
.BR gerantd (1)
runs it for every VM it starts with
.BR Notifications=yes ,
so it is rarely run by hand.
.PP
It waits for the agent, retrying every second, and reconnects when the agent
restarts or the VM reboots. When the connection ends, or the relay gets
.B SIGTERM
or
.BR SIGINT ,
it closes every notification it showed.
.SS How notifications look
.IP \(bu 2
The application name gets the VM's name:
.BR "Firefox (debian)" .
.IP \(bu
If
.BR carte (1)
has a launcher for the sending application, the notification names it in
its
.B desktop\-entry
hint, so the host shows the launcher's name and icon and can turn that
application's notifications off on its own.
.IP \(bu
Icons are read in the guest and written to
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/sonnette/vm/
for the host's server, until the notification closes.
.IP \(bu
Hints that mean the same on the host are passed on:
.BR urgency ,
.BR category ,
.BR resident ,
.BR transient ,
.BR action\-icons ,
.BR sound\-name ,
.BR suppress\-sound .
Others are dropped.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on failure, 2 for a usage error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/sonnette/vm/
Icons of the notifications on screen.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/garnish/vm/sonnette.log
The relay's output, when
.B gerantd
runs it.
.SH SECURITY
Everything from the guest is untrusted. The relay cuts names, summaries,
bodies, actions and hints to fixed lengths and keeps at most 16 actions;
drops
.B <a>
and
.B <img>
tags from the body, keeping a link's text; accepts icons only as PNG or SVG
and pixel data only as 8-bit RGB or RGBA; and lets a VM show 20 new
notifications at once and 2 per second after that (replacing one doesn't
count). The application name always has the VM's name in it, so a guest
can't pass its notifications off as the host's.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sonnette\-agent (1),
.BR gerantd (1),
.BR carte (1),
.BR garnish (7)
